(PRC-15 — fstype "none" with options "move" is recognised and translated
 into MS_MOVE.
 Also covers: PRC-16 (options "bind" -> MS_BIND).
 SAFETY / LIMIT: unprivileged, so both calls return EPERM. That proves the
 pattern PARSES and reaches mount(2); it does NOT prove the flag
 translation, because the syscall never gets far enough to distinguish
 MS_MOVE from a plain mount. Confirming MS_MOVE/MS_BIND needs either root
 or a user namespace, neither of which this map had.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-15.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the move pattern set the error flag
   the bind pattern set the error flag
   both patterns compiled and reached the syscall
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_move".
Mount "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_move" at "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_move" with type "none" with options "move".
On error print "the move pattern set the error flag".
Mount "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_move" at "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_move" with type "none" with options "bind".
On error print "the bind pattern set the error flag".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_move".
print "both patterns compiled and reached the syscall".
